I am thinking...: OK so the serializer starts with:
- `start` = beginning of buffer (uninitialized memory from `buf.alloc`)
- `end` = start + size
- `head` = start (grows forward during serialization)
- `tail` = end (grows backward during pop_pack)

When `push()` is called, it creates a new object that starts at the current `head`. Then the serialization operations (embed, extend, etc.) move `head` forward. When `pop_pack()` is called, it knows the object's range as `obj->head` to `obj->tail` (which is current `head`). Then it copies the data by moving `head` back to `obj->head`.

Wait, I don't think data is copied. Let me re-read `pop_pack`:

```cpp
objidx_t pop_pack ()
{
    object_t *obj = current;
    if (unlikely (!obj)) return 0;
    current = current->next;
    obj->tail = head;
    obj->next = nullptr;
    unsigned len = obj->tail - obj->head;
    head = obj->head; /* Rewind head. */
    ...
    objidx_t objidx = packed_map.get (obj);
    if (objidx)
    {
        obj->fini ();
        return objidx;
    }
    ...
    obj->head = tail - len;
    memmove (obj->head, head, len);
    tail -= len;
    ...
}
```

So `pop_pack()`:
1. Sets `obj->tail = head` (current write position = end of object data)
2. `len = obj->tail - obj->head` (object data length)
3. `head = obj->head` (rewind head to before the object)
4. Checks `packed_map.get(obj)` - this hashes the object content at `obj->head` through `obj->tail`
5. If not found, moves data from head area to tail area

The key insight: `allocate_size` always memsets to 0:
```cpp
template <typename Type>
Type *allocate_size (unsigned int size)
{
    ...
    Type *ret = reinterpret_cast<Type *> (this->head);
    this->head += size;
    memset ((void*) ret, 0, size);
    return ret;
}
```

So any space allocated via `allocate_size` is zeroed. But what if there's a path where data is written to the serialization buffer without going through `allocate_size`?

Wait, let me look at `embed` more carefully:

```cpp
template <typename Type>
Type *embed (const Type &obj)
{ return embed (hb_addressof (obj)); }

template <typename Type>
Type *embed (const Type *obj)
{
    unsigned int size = obj->get_size ();
    Type *ret = this->allocate_size<Type> (size);
    if (unlikely (!ret)) return nullptr;
    memcpy (ret, obj, size);
    return ret;
